# Spec §5.5 (schedule), with §4.1 (schedule field) and §5.1–§5.3.
# A task with a schedule can only be completed within its daily time window
# [from, to) (from inclusive, to exclusive; it does not cross midnight).
# T = instant at which it would become pending without a schedule: one-off,
#   createdAt; relative, V = U + interval (never completed, createdAt); calendar,
#   00:00 of N.
# A (available) = T if it falls within the window of its day; otherwise, the
#   from of the next window. C (close) = the to of that window.
# Overdue = the earlier of C and the overdue instant without a schedule (relative:
#   V + interval; one-off with a due date: the to of the window of the due date's
#   day). It wins over everything else, also before A.
#   now ≥ overdue: atrasada (also outside the windows).
#   now < A: en espera; progress = (now − start of waiting) / (A −
#     start of waiting); start of waiting from §5.2/§5.3 (one-off: createdAt).
#   A ≤ now < C: pendiente.
#   One-off without a due date, now ≥ C: outside a window, en espera
#     until the from of the next one (progress from the to of the previous one);
#     inside, pendiente. Never atrasada.
#   One-off with a due date: as without a due date until the overdue instant.
# Skewed clocks (now < U): en espera with progress 0 (§5.2).
# Progress is a fraction between 0 and 1, compared exactly.
# Reference week: Monday 2026-07-13 to Sunday 2026-07-19.
Feature: Status with schedule

  # Status with schedule 1
  # One-off without a due date created before the window (or at night): en
  # espera until the from of the next window, with progress from createdAt.
  Scenario Outline: Status with schedule 1
    Given a one-off task without a due date created on <created>
    And the task can be completed from <from> to <to>
    When I query the status on <now>
    Then the status is en espera
    And the progress is <progress>

    Examples:
      | created             | from  | to    | now                 | progress |
      | 2026-07-15T06:00:00 | 08:00 | 11:00 | 2026-07-15T07:00:00 | 0.5      |
      | 2026-07-15T12:00:00 | 08:00 | 11:00 | 2026-07-16T02:00:00 | 0.7      |
      | 2026-07-15T20:00:00 | 21:00 | 23:00 | 2026-07-15T20:30:00 | 0.5      |

